WEBVTT

00:21.724 --> 00:23.704
Howard!

00:25.524 --> 00:28.404
Ray... You have...

00:28.694 --> 00:29.654
to live.

00:52.484 --> 00:55.134
Is that... overheating?

01:14.924 --> 01:22.804
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

02:21.814 --> 02:25.004
<b>Episode 1
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest 
Sorcerer Enters the Academy of Sorcery</b>

02:30.474 --> 02:31.894
It really is huge.

02:36.284 --> 02:38.014
Let's see...

02:38.014 --> 02:39.844
Which way is the auditorium?

02:43.954 --> 02:44.914
Apologies,

02:45.694 --> 02:46.694
my lady.

02:49.834 --> 02:51.974
Oh, that's all right.

02:51.974 --> 02:55.864
But I'm not sure it's a good idea to 
suddenly stop in the middle of the path.

02:56.254 --> 02:58.374
I apologize. I'm new here.

02:58.634 --> 03:02.614
What? But didn't all new students 
move onto campus two days ago?

03:03.574 --> 03:08.384
I heard there'd be just one moving in 
on the day of the entrance ceremony!

03:08.384 --> 03:10.594
One who descends from neither 
aristocrat nor sorcerer,

03:10.594 --> 03:13.224
but is born of an ordinary family.

03:13.224 --> 03:15.524
Ordinary?!

03:15.524 --> 03:16.474
Wait, that's him?

03:16.474 --> 03:18.674
First one since the school 
was founded, I heard.

03:17.974 --> 03:19.724
Pretty bold for an ordinary.

03:19.724 --> 03:21.404
Did he get in on connections?

03:19.964 --> 03:23.424
I-I can't believe an 
<i>ordinary</i> just touched me...

03:23.954 --> 03:24.494
Wanda!

03:24.494 --> 03:26.194
Wanda! Keep it together!

03:26.194 --> 03:27.954
It's okay! Everything's okay!

03:27.954 --> 03:29.314
Wanda!

03:27.954 --> 03:29.944
So you're Ray White?

03:31.224 --> 03:32.164
And you are?

03:32.164 --> 03:34.194
Albert Alium.

03:34.524 --> 03:37.874
I'm Ray White. May I call you "Mr. Alium"?

03:38.464 --> 03:41.304
Only nobles are allowed 
to attend this school,

03:41.304 --> 03:44.994
or, at the very least, 
those descended from sorcerers.

03:44.994 --> 03:47.404
That's because the Arnold Academy of Sorcery

03:47.404 --> 03:50.434
has ancient and honorable 
origins as a school for nobles!

03:50.434 --> 03:52.914
Yeah, that's right! Totally right!

03:52.914 --> 03:55.684
I don't know what strings 
you pulled to get here,

03:55.684 --> 03:59.654
but this is no place for 
an ordinary like you!

03:59.654 --> 04:00.974
You tell 'im!

04:01.304 --> 04:05.814
That's unfortunate. There are many 
things I want to learn at this academy.

04:06.024 --> 04:07.234
Why, you—

04:09.724 --> 04:11.614
You worthless ordinary!

04:11.884 --> 04:12.964
Enough!

04:13.844 --> 04:14.744
Tch.

04:18.584 --> 04:20.124
Whoa! She's...

04:20.714 --> 04:22.584
From one of the top three noble families.

04:22.864 --> 04:25.374
Al, maybe you should stop...

04:25.634 --> 04:26.954
Lady Rose!

04:27.784 --> 04:29.004
She's such a treasure!

04:29.624 --> 04:30.484
Rose?

04:30.484 --> 04:31.504
Hmph!

04:32.224 --> 04:36.704
I will never accept an ordinary like you!

04:37.724 --> 04:39.944
Hey! Wait up, Al!

04:38.744 --> 04:40.614
Are you all right?

04:40.614 --> 04:42.194
Yeah. Thanks.

04:45.494 --> 04:46.984
I'm Amelia Rose.

04:47.334 --> 04:48.564
Miss Rose.

04:49.244 --> 04:50.704
I'm Ray White.

04:50.704 --> 04:52.114
Feel free to call me "Ray."

04:52.434 --> 04:55.464
And you can call me "Amelia," as well.

04:56.474 --> 04:59.384
You're the first ordinary 
to attend this academy.

04:59.384 --> 05:00.704
That's a big deal.

05:00.984 --> 05:02.984
Clearly, your talents have been recognized.

05:02.984 --> 05:04.494
I couldn't be more grateful.

05:04.494 --> 05:05.854
So, Ray...

05:05.854 --> 05:06.834
What is it?

05:07.514 --> 05:10.774
If you have any problems 
at all, you can talk to me.

05:18.624 --> 05:20.344
Now, a word from our principal.

05:23.364 --> 05:24.694
Welcome, students.

05:25.984 --> 05:28.324
The Arnold Academy of Sorcery

05:28.324 --> 05:30.394
is among the finest schools in the world.

05:30.824 --> 05:32.754
All of you who stand here today

05:32.754 --> 05:35.904
have been acknowledged for 
your talents as sorcerers.

05:36.164 --> 05:39.564
But do not be prideful. 
Hard work is still a must.

05:39.564 --> 05:41.414
Spare no blood, sweat, or tears.

05:41.714 --> 05:46.794
One's skills are a product of their innate 
talent, environment, and hard work.

05:47.314 --> 05:50.074
Many sorcerers, despite remarkable 
talents and favorable environments,

05:50.074 --> 05:53.294
lose heart and let their 
abilities waste away.

05:53.794 --> 05:56.104
Thus, I tell you this:

05:56.784 --> 06:00.304
Put in the effort to become 
first-rate sorcerers.

06:02.644 --> 06:07.184
I am Abbie Garnet, the principal 
of the Arnold Academy of Sorcery.

06:08.294 --> 06:09.484
Thank you.

06:09.944 --> 06:12.734
Thank you for that speech, Principal.

06:13.094 --> 06:14.024
Next,

06:14.304 --> 06:16.694
a word from the representative 
of incoming students.

06:20.914 --> 06:24.044
I am Amelia Rose, 
representative of the incoming students.

06:24.354 --> 06:29.044
I am proud to have been accepted 
to this prestigious academy.

06:29.324 --> 06:33.504
However, this is not our destination, 
but rather our starting point.

06:33.814 --> 06:39.054
I'm sure many difficulties 
lie on the road ahead of us.

06:39.564 --> 06:42.954
But now that I am a student of this academy,

06:42.954 --> 06:45.724
I intend to face all of them head-on.

06:45.724 --> 06:48.354
As the principal said a moment ago,

06:48.654 --> 06:51.354
to continually work hard 
and master our sorcery

06:51.354 --> 06:54.674
is the mission we have undertaken.

06:55.884 --> 06:56.904
That's him?

06:56.904 --> 06:58.524
Look, it's the guy everyone's talking about.

06:58.524 --> 06:59.424
Really?

06:59.424 --> 07:00.604
Silence.

07:01.034 --> 07:02.944
This is the last student to join the class,

07:02.944 --> 07:04.614
the one I've told you about.

07:05.094 --> 07:06.364
I'm Ray White.

07:06.674 --> 07:09.914
As I'm sure many of you know, 
I come from an ordinary family.

07:10.824 --> 07:13.464
I've heard I'm the first ordinary 
at this school since it was founded,

07:14.134 --> 07:19.634
but I intend to put forth my best effort 
as a sorcerer throughout my time here.

07:19.634 --> 07:20.554
I hope we can work together.

07:24.144 --> 07:28.514
Okay, White. Sorry to just throw you 
into this, but you know the situation.

07:28.514 --> 07:31.184
You can introduce yourself to 
your classmates individually.

07:31.184 --> 07:32.564
Yes, Instructor.

07:33.384 --> 07:37.064
It's Helena Grady. You can call me Miss Gray.

07:37.064 --> 07:39.554
My apologies, Instructor Gray.

07:39.554 --> 07:41.174
Must you be so rigid?

07:41.174 --> 07:42.924
Okay, fine. Go on and sit down.

07:42.924 --> 07:43.824
Yes, ma'am.

07:44.804 --> 07:46.834
Looking forward to working with you, Ray.

07:46.834 --> 07:48.324
Same here, Amelia.

07:48.594 --> 07:50.684
Why is Lady Rose talking to him?

07:49.384 --> 07:51.384
Wait, why? Why?!

07:50.684 --> 07:52.834
One of the three top families 
is interested in him?

07:55.284 --> 07:56.834
Ordinary...

08:13.174 --> 08:14.304
White!

08:14.994 --> 08:15.854
White!

08:24.194 --> 08:26.574
Class is in session, White.

08:26.964 --> 08:28.744
You need to pay attention.

08:28.744 --> 08:30.044
I apologize.

08:30.384 --> 08:31.584
To get back on topic...

08:31.954 --> 08:34.194
We were discussing sorcerer ranks.

08:34.194 --> 08:35.464
Do you know what they are, Rose?

08:35.814 --> 08:36.594
Yes, ma'am.

08:37.964 --> 08:40.764
There are five ranks established 
by the Society of Sorcery:

08:41.244 --> 08:44.424
bronze, silver, gold, platinum...

08:44.644 --> 08:47.674
and grand, the rank regarded as sacred.

08:48.084 --> 08:49.524
Correct.

08:49.524 --> 08:53.334
Only seven grand sorcerers 
exist at any one time.

08:53.334 --> 08:56.524
These seven, who have mastered 
the very essence of sorcery,

08:56.524 --> 08:59.074
are known as the seven greatest 
sorcerers in the world.

08:59.074 --> 09:02.484
They are the pinnacle of sorcery 
that all sorcerers strive to match.

09:03.004 --> 09:07.284
The very existence of the seven greatest 
sorcerers is shrouded in mystery,

09:07.284 --> 09:10.494
but a few details about them 
are known to the public.

09:10.784 --> 09:14.754
First, our very own principal, Abbie Garnet,

09:14.754 --> 09:16.504
is the Blaze Sorcerer.

09:16.954 --> 09:20.274
Next, the Spellbinding 
Sorcerer, Carol Caroline.

09:20.684 --> 09:25.944
She's the most well-known of the 
seven as a researcher of sorcery.

09:26.364 --> 09:30.664
In fact, she's just about the only one 
who really puts herself out there.

09:31.894 --> 09:36.894
And then there's the one known as 
the hero of the Far East War...

09:36.894 --> 09:38.894
The Iceblade Sorcerer.

09:39.104 --> 09:40.104
Exactly.

09:40.104 --> 09:42.904
The Iceblade Sorcerer is the one who vanished

09:42.904 --> 09:45.674
after bringing an end to the Far East War.

09:46.034 --> 09:48.144
Nothing is known about the rest of the seven.

09:48.144 --> 09:50.124
Not even their aliases.

09:50.594 --> 09:52.914
But as I said earlier,

09:52.914 --> 09:57.794
so long as you attend this academy, 
you should be aware that the destination

09:57.794 --> 10:02.544
at the end of your path is the rank of 
grand sorcerer, one of the great seven.

10:02.544 --> 10:03.954
Miss Gray.

10:03.954 --> 10:05.144
What is it, Alium?

10:06.214 --> 10:10.104
If the goal we strive for is to be 
one of the seven great sorcerers,

10:10.104 --> 10:13.414
then why is there an ordinary at this school?

10:13.414 --> 10:14.244
That's right.

10:13.804 --> 10:15.414
Why is there an ordinary?

10:14.244 --> 10:15.414
It doesn't make sense.

10:16.884 --> 10:19.914
The only students here are those 
who passed the mandated exam,

10:19.914 --> 10:24.064
as well as an in-person interview 
to be approved as students.

10:24.064 --> 10:26.564
Whether they are noble or 
ordinary means nothing.

10:26.564 --> 10:27.364
Tch.

10:32.124 --> 10:34.304
Now, it's time to practice some sorcery.

10:34.304 --> 10:36.264
You might not think it necessary anymore,

10:36.264 --> 10:39.164
but you will be starting from 
the most basic of exercises.

10:39.424 --> 10:41.074
Do not underestimate the basics.

10:41.074 --> 10:44.624
Even the seven great 
sorcerers are no exception.

10:44.624 --> 10:45.704
Now, Rose...

10:45.704 --> 10:46.174
Yes, ma'am.

10:46.434 --> 10:48.174
What is "sorcery"?

10:48.444 --> 10:52.384
Sorcery refers to the art of 
reconstructing prima materia,

10:52.384 --> 10:55.554
the primary building block 
of matter in our world.

10:55.884 --> 10:57.864
Very good. That's right.

10:58.554 --> 11:01.814
And at the very core of 
sorcery is the code theory.

11:02.984 --> 11:06.634
<i>Prima materia, encoding, material code.</i>

11:07.074 --> 11:09.604
First, you encode prima materia,

11:09.604 --> 11:11.444
or in other words, turn it into code.

11:11.444 --> 11:14.934
At this stage, there is still excess data.

11:14.934 --> 11:16.114
So...

11:16.114 --> 11:20.204
<i>Material code, decoding, material code.</i>

11:20.204 --> 11:21.974
You remove the excess by decoding,

11:21.974 --> 11:26.064
put the data back in order, 
and move to the processing stage.

11:26.504 --> 11:28.794
<i>Material code, processing.</i>

11:29.144 --> 11:32.764
Here, you can add or remove more data.

11:32.764 --> 11:34.944
Finally, you manifest it.

11:34.944 --> 11:37.264
<i>Embodiment, material.</i>

11:39.914 --> 11:41.824
These are the fundamentals of sorcery.

11:43.224 --> 11:45.684
Additionally, anything you have made...

11:46.954 --> 11:49.254
you can also erase.

11:50.004 --> 11:54.574
Sorcery is a theoretical phenomenon derived 
from the understanding of technique.

11:55.004 --> 11:58.304
Any questions about what 
I've explained thus far?

11:58.304 --> 11:59.494
I have one, ma'am.

11:59.784 --> 12:01.574
You do, Rose? Very well.

12:02.104 --> 12:06.164
Are there any limits on the things 
reconstructed by prima materia?

12:06.484 --> 12:09.584
No, strictly speaking, there are no limits.

12:09.584 --> 12:12.174
It all depends on the 
sorcerer's own capability.

12:12.854 --> 12:17.434
Sorcery is, primarily, the art 
of creating matter or phenomena.

12:17.884 --> 12:20.554
Matter can be separated into four categories.

12:22.014 --> 12:23.164
Solids.

12:25.604 --> 12:26.774
Liquids.

12:28.354 --> 12:29.444
Gases.

12:30.764 --> 12:33.234
And finally, plasma.

12:33.634 --> 12:36.954
Anything else is classified as a phenomenon.

12:40.264 --> 12:41.614
Anyone else?

12:41.614 --> 12:42.964
U-Um...

12:43.704 --> 12:46.774
When you erased the ice roses earlier,

12:46.774 --> 12:49.334
did you use anti-material code?

12:49.334 --> 12:55.344
No. There is no sorcerer who 
uses anti-material code.

12:55.834 --> 12:59.594
Ainsworth's twofold code theory 
is doctorate-level material.

13:00.014 --> 13:01.804
Students don't need to understand it yet.

13:03.604 --> 13:05.314
Now for some exercises.

13:09.414 --> 13:11.774
<i>Prima materia, encoding.</i>

13:11.774 --> 13:13.134
<i>Material code.</i>

13:13.134 --> 13:15.464
<i>Material code, decoding.</i>

13:13.864 --> 13:16.424
<i>Material code, processing.</i>

13:16.964 --> 13:18.954
<i>Embodiment, material.</i>

13:22.084 --> 13:25.554
I knew you could do it, 
Lady Rose! Magnificent!

13:24.834 --> 13:26.784
Th-Thanks...

13:25.554 --> 13:28.674
Leave it to a lady of one 
of the highest noble families.

13:26.784 --> 13:30.584
I love it so, so, so, so, so, so much!

13:28.314 --> 13:30.104
Uh, yeah...

13:28.674 --> 13:30.584
On the other hand...

13:33.424 --> 13:35.674
Hmm... I see.

13:35.974 --> 13:37.604
What was that supposed to be?

13:37.604 --> 13:39.424
That was a child's sorcery.

13:39.424 --> 13:41.724
But didn't the teacher 
say he passed the exam?

13:41.724 --> 13:43.544
What's his deal, anyway?

13:43.544 --> 13:45.144
He's totally useless.

13:47.734 --> 13:49.364
Ordinary...

13:49.364 --> 13:51.104
Whoa... Al?!

13:51.634 --> 13:53.814
<i>As a member of the Alium household,</i>

13:53.814 --> 13:59.184
<i>I refuse to acknowledge the existence 
of a talentless Withered Wizard!</i>

14:02.334 --> 14:05.224
This is definitely a 
historical school building.

14:05.224 --> 14:07.164
Its construction is flawless.

14:12.744 --> 14:13.834
Looking for Ainsworth?

14:13.834 --> 14:14.934
Huh?! Ah...

14:14.934 --> 14:17.544
You asked about it in class earlier.

14:17.544 --> 14:19.734
Oh... Um, I...

14:19.734 --> 14:22.394
Sorry for asking out of nowhere. 
I'm Ray White.

14:22.394 --> 14:23.824
Oh... um...

14:23.824 --> 14:25.864
I'm Elisa Griffith.

14:25.864 --> 14:27.944
Nice to meet you, Miss Griffith.

14:27.944 --> 14:29.694
You can call me "Ray."

14:29.694 --> 14:32.794
Oh... And you can call me "Elisa."

14:33.114 --> 14:35.664
Once more, nice to meet you, Elisa.

14:35.664 --> 14:36.894
Same to you.

14:38.494 --> 14:40.904
Dr. Ainsworth is my role model.

14:41.604 --> 14:44.144
So that's why you asked about 
the twofold code theory.

14:44.144 --> 14:47.454
Yeah. I want to be just like her.

14:47.454 --> 14:51.264
That's amazing. She's a top-ranking 
researcher of sorcery.

14:52.034 --> 14:54.604
Well, it's just a dream.

14:55.264 --> 14:58.504
Do you like Dr. Ainsworth, too?

14:58.504 --> 15:01.984
Yeah. I love her from the bottom of my heart.

15:01.984 --> 15:06.614
Really?! Wow! I've never met 
any other Ainsers my age!

15:06.854 --> 15:08.594
Ainsers?

15:08.594 --> 15:09.394
Oh...

15:10.014 --> 15:13.484
That means... fans of Dr. Ainsworth.

15:13.484 --> 15:16.414
Never heard that before. 
There's actually a word for them, huh?

15:16.974 --> 15:20.424
I'm sorry for getting so carried away.

15:20.424 --> 15:22.914
I don't mind. Why, though?

15:22.914 --> 15:23.674
Why what?

15:24.354 --> 15:26.674
You have such beautiful hair.

15:26.674 --> 15:27.404
Huh?!

15:29.214 --> 15:29.844
Elisa...

15:31.514 --> 15:32.904
is there some reason?

15:34.474 --> 15:37.384
Well... don't you think my ears are weird?

15:37.384 --> 15:38.444
They're not weird.

15:39.204 --> 15:40.444
They're lovely.

15:41.084 --> 15:44.024
So you're an elf... no, a half-elf, right?

15:44.544 --> 15:46.534
My mother is an elf.

15:46.764 --> 15:49.724
I've been made fun of all my 
life because of these ears.

15:49.724 --> 15:51.684
I think you're beautiful, Elisa.

15:52.144 --> 15:52.534
Huh?!

15:53.284 --> 15:55.994
So what need is there to hide them?

15:58.274 --> 16:02.644
I-I'm glad you think so, I guess.

16:03.644 --> 16:06.144
You seem very mature, Ray.

16:06.144 --> 16:07.054
Do I?

16:07.054 --> 16:10.054
Yeah. You don't look like you're my age.

16:10.634 --> 16:14.974
Jeez, kid, you act way too old for your age.

16:15.324 --> 16:16.564
You're too mature!

16:17.534 --> 16:20.194
I guess I do get that a lot.

16:20.544 --> 16:21.804
I thought so.

16:23.924 --> 16:26.224
Thank you for talking to me today, Ray.

16:26.224 --> 16:29.034
Same to you. I look forward to 
spending more time together.

16:29.304 --> 16:31.774
Um... See you tomorrow.

16:31.774 --> 16:32.484
Yeah.

16:37.064 --> 16:38.124
Pardon me.

16:38.124 --> 16:40.664
I've been waiting for you, Ray White.

16:42.844 --> 16:44.594
You're Evi Armstrong?

16:45.044 --> 16:47.184
Call me "Evi," Ray.

16:47.544 --> 16:50.394
Oh? I appreciate the invitation.

16:50.394 --> 16:52.964
I'm not like those noble kids.

16:52.964 --> 16:55.304
I don't care if you're an ordinary.

16:55.764 --> 16:58.314
There's only one thing I believe in.

17:03.054 --> 17:05.814
I knew it! Just like I thought!

17:05.814 --> 17:08.114
Evi, you're...

17:10.704 --> 17:12.204
You've got some nice bulk.

17:12.914 --> 17:14.254
Same to you.

17:16.044 --> 17:17.944
You're welcome here, Ray!

17:17.944 --> 17:19.634
Thanks! Nice to meet you!

17:30.244 --> 17:31.104
Huh?

17:33.114 --> 17:34.704
Sorry about that.

17:34.704 --> 17:36.774
I wasn't expecting anyone to be here.

17:36.774 --> 17:38.254
It's all right.

17:38.564 --> 17:41.034
Running so early in the 
morning is very impressive.

17:41.034 --> 17:43.274
Are you an incoming student?

17:43.274 --> 17:46.114
Yes. My name is Ray White.

17:46.114 --> 17:47.774
Oh! You're Ray White?

17:47.774 --> 17:49.274
You know of me?

17:49.274 --> 17:53.494
The academy's first ordinary. 
You're very famous.

17:53.494 --> 17:54.784
I'm honored.

17:54.994 --> 17:58.734
My name is Rebecca Bradley. I'm a third-year.

17:58.734 --> 18:00.794
Feel free to call me "Rebecca."

18:01.064 --> 18:03.294
I'll do that, Rebecca.

18:03.524 --> 18:05.124
Good, Ray.

18:06.834 --> 18:10.554
Bradley? That's one of the 
top three noble families!

18:10.554 --> 18:11.804
Top three noble families?

18:12.024 --> 18:13.824
You really don't know?

18:13.824 --> 18:16.104
Well, I grew up in the countryside.

18:16.104 --> 18:17.864
I don't know much about the nobility.

18:18.334 --> 18:21.224
Rose, Bradley, and Olgren.

18:21.794 --> 18:25.334
Those three families are as 
powerful as the royal family,

18:25.334 --> 18:28.174
with just as much influence over politics,

18:28.174 --> 18:29.914
the economy, and everything 
else in this country.

18:30.234 --> 18:32.154
That's who the top three noble families are.

18:32.154 --> 18:33.994
So Amelia is...

18:33.994 --> 18:37.084
The eldest daughter of the Rose family, 
the highest of the three.

18:37.084 --> 18:41.784
She's got spotless integrity, high morals, 
and first-rate sorcerer skills.

18:41.784 --> 18:44.794
She's a genuine, born-and-bred lady.

18:47.354 --> 18:49.214
Evi, you can go on ahead.

18:49.214 --> 18:50.024
Huh?

18:50.024 --> 18:51.844
The instructor wanted to see me.

18:51.844 --> 18:55.114
Okay. Remember, first period 
is practical swordsmanship.

18:55.114 --> 18:56.864
We'll have to change, so get there early.

18:56.864 --> 18:57.594
Right.

19:00.144 --> 19:01.974
Whoa!

19:04.364 --> 19:05.934
Are you all right?

19:08.104 --> 19:10.734
Hey! Watch where you're going!

19:10.734 --> 19:14.114
My apologies. I was just 
walking like normal, though...

19:14.114 --> 19:16.834
Well, I was running because 
I was kind of in a hurry!

19:16.834 --> 19:18.554
So you should have moved aside!

19:18.554 --> 19:22.454
Uh-huh... That's awfully 
unreasonable, but I do apologize.

19:22.964 --> 19:25.644
You're weird. Wait...

19:25.644 --> 19:27.344
Aren't you that ordinary?!

19:27.344 --> 19:29.214
I'm Ray White. Nice to meet you,

19:29.524 --> 19:31.624
my charming, pigtailed lady.

19:32.404 --> 19:35.124
Well, you certainly know just where to look!

19:35.124 --> 19:37.994
You actually recognized the 
greatness of these pigtails!

19:37.994 --> 19:38.844
Really?

19:39.754 --> 19:42.004
I am the first and the last,

19:42.004 --> 19:44.394
the girl of transcendent, raging cuteness...

19:44.604 --> 19:48.944
The girl who loves and 
is loved by pigtails...

19:48.944 --> 19:53.024
I am Claris Cleve...

19:53.024 --> 19:54.964
land!

19:56.814 --> 19:58.684
Wow, how nice.

19:59.074 --> 20:01.604
I'm not familiar with 
the "Cleve Land" family,

20:01.604 --> 20:03.414
but I hope we can get along.

20:03.414 --> 20:06.314
What?! You don't know the Clevelands?

20:06.314 --> 20:10.164
I'm sorry. I grew up in the countryside, 
so I don't know much about the nobility.

20:10.394 --> 20:13.674
I see. Well, that's fine... yeah.

20:13.904 --> 20:16.644
It's a pretty well-known family, though...

20:16.644 --> 20:18.964
I see... You don't know us, huh?

20:18.964 --> 20:21.674
But I'm sure it's a beautiful family.

20:21.674 --> 20:23.684
That's clear just from looking at you.

20:24.194 --> 20:25.104
You can tell?!

20:25.544 --> 20:27.984
Oh, very well, then!

20:27.984 --> 20:31.424
I'll grant you special permission 
to call me "Claris," Ray!

20:31.424 --> 20:34.644
I appreciate that. 
I hope we'll get along, Claris.

20:35.364 --> 20:37.764
I suppose I'll let you get along with me!

20:38.564 --> 20:40.904
Anyway, weren't you in a hurry?

20:40.904 --> 20:42.044
Oh, crap!

20:42.044 --> 20:44.084
Well, bye! See you later!

20:44.084 --> 20:44.624
Okay.

20:49.104 --> 20:50.904
Welcome, Ray.

20:51.604 --> 20:53.624
It's good to see you again, Colonel.

20:53.624 --> 20:57.224
None of that, now. You and I have 
both retired from the service.

20:57.224 --> 20:59.134
What shall I call you, then?

20:59.634 --> 21:00.724
Just "Abbie."

21:00.724 --> 21:02.914
Understood, Abbie.

21:05.374 --> 21:06.784
You haven't changed.

21:06.784 --> 21:09.524
That part of you is so much like him.

21:10.704 --> 21:13.544
It brings back memories, doesn't it, Abbie?

21:13.544 --> 21:14.464
Uh, hey...

21:15.554 --> 21:18.604
Albert Alium and Ray White.

21:19.544 --> 21:21.654
This is no more than a mock battle.

21:21.654 --> 21:23.864
If it looks like it's getting 
dangerous, I'll stop you.

21:24.234 --> 21:26.034
Look, it's the Withered.

21:25.124 --> 21:27.114
Hah, the Withered!

21:26.324 --> 21:28.034
Who the heck said he was good, anyway?

21:28.294 --> 21:29.444
Withered?

21:30.284 --> 21:32.184
They call him the "Withered Wizard."

21:32.184 --> 21:32.874
Huh?

21:32.874 --> 21:35.534
I'm Ray's bosom buddy, Evi.

21:35.534 --> 21:38.844
Oh, well, hello... But what does that mean?

21:38.844 --> 21:40.614
It's wordplay.

21:40.614 --> 21:42.514
"Withered" and "Wizard"...

21:42.974 --> 21:45.104
They're practically the same word.

21:45.104 --> 21:46.894
Oh, I get it.

21:46.894 --> 21:48.224
<i>Ray...</i>

21:49.024 --> 21:50.804
Okay, are you both ready?

21:50.804 --> 21:53.824
<i>Someone who can't even use sorcery...</i>

21:53.824 --> 21:54.654
Begin!

21:54.654 --> 21:57.064
...has no right to stand 
on the same level as me!

22:03.244 --> 22:04.264
No way!

22:04.264 --> 22:05.504
Not bad, man!

22:05.504 --> 22:06.494
Impossible!

22:06.724 --> 22:07.534
Ray!

22:08.174 --> 22:10.864
That doesn't have too much influence on me.

22:11.924 --> 22:14.084
You... You...

22:14.634 --> 22:17.334
You damned Withered!

22:25.024 --> 22:25.904
No way...

22:25.904 --> 22:27.044
For real?

22:29.264 --> 22:32.564
I'm glad to see you enjoying 
your student life,

22:34.604 --> 22:35.964
Ray White...

22:36.954 --> 22:38.944
the Iceblade Sorcerer.

23:50.014 --> 23:54.484
Students! This is the preview for 
<i>The Iceblade Sorcerer Shall Rule the World</i>!

23:50.014 --> 23:55.004
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

23:50.014 --> 23:55.004
<b>~ Next Episode Preview ~</b>

23:55.004 --> 23:56.924
Having quietly made up his mind,

23:56.924 --> 23:59.304
Ray heads to the place that's a sanctuary
 for fierce, impassioned muscle men,

23:59.304 --> 24:02.474
and a garden for pure, elegant young ladies.

24:02.474 --> 24:06.114
"The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest 
Sorcerer Begins His Practical Exercises."

24:05.514 --> 24:10.264
<b>Episode 2
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest 
Sorcerer Begins His Practical Exercises</b>

24:06.694 --> 24:09.274
Abbie Garnet, signing off!
